    "recap": {
      "text": "Banner night nearly turned bleak in Seattle. Sam Darnold hurt his hip on the opening possession, and the Seahawks offense sputtered behind Drew Lock, trailing 10-3 entering the fourth quarter. Then the defense hijacked the game, picking off Drake Maye three times in the final period, and Lock answered with a 45-yard strike to Jaxon Smith-Njigba before Jason Myers punched through a 26-yarder for the lead. Seattle 13, New England 10 — a grind-it-out finish that Mike Macdonald credited to a team that refused to flinch.",
      "blurbSource": "llm"
